WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.090
In 2023, income per person
in Guyana was 46,959 dollars,

2
00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:10.410
in 2021 purchasing power parity terms.

3
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:14.150
In Sri Lanka: 12,616.

4
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.950
Now look at the Human Development Index.

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.050
Guyana: 0.776.

6
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.310
Sri Lanka: 0.776.

7
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.750
Both countries rank 89th in the world.

8
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:30.510
How can more than three and a half
times the income buy the same score?

9
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.210
A mistake in the data?

10
00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:36.850
In this mission, you'll judge development
against the UN's 17 Sustainable Development

11
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.170
Goals and their 169 targets.

12
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:45.290
Then you'll take apart two indices, the
HDI and the Gender Inequality Index,

13
00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:48.170
and test their validity and reliability.

14
00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:53.630
Your mission: explain why Guyana and
Sri Lanka have exactly the same HDI.
